# Local Worker secrets for `wrangler dev` / `opennextjs-cloudflare preview`.
# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored); never commit a value.
#
# The service-role key: server code only (the Paddle webhook's sync and
# /api/health). In stage and prod every deploy sets it as a Worker secret from
# the Supabase root's wiring document; here it is yours.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# Paddle's server-side keys. Unset, the dashboard's subscription and payment
# views say "Paddle is not connected." and the webhook answers 503. In stage
# and prod they are the product's Orun secrets, which the deploy pushes to the
# Worker as Worker secrets (README, "Connecting Paddle").
# PADDLE_API_KEY=pdl_sdbx_apikey_***
# PADDLE_NOTIFICATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET=pdl_ntfset_***
#
# Paddle's public values — the client-side token and the environment — are
# read by the BROWSER, so `next build` inlines them: export them before
# `pnpm build` (or put them in .env.local for `next dev`), not here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=test_***
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV=sandbox
#
# The Supabase URL and anon key, and the site's origin, are wrangler vars
# (rendered into wrangler.jsonc, which the build inlines); put real values
# here only to point a local Worker at a real project's server side.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
